Write a method in PascalABC.NET for finding the longest common subsequence of two strings. The longest common subsequence is defined as the longest sequence of characters that appear in the same order in both strings, but not necessarily consecutively. 

Additionally, the method should handle the case where either or both of the input strings are null or empty. If either string is null or empty, the method should return an empty string as the longest common subsequence.

Furthermore, the method should also handle the case where the input strings contain special characters and numbers. The method should only consider the alphabetical characters in finding the longest common subsequence and ignore any special characters and numbers present in the strings.

string s1 = "ABC123DEF"; 
string s2 = "AC#D$EF";

