Here is a PascalABC.NET program that uses a divide and conquer algorithm to find the second smallest element in an array, without using any built-in methods or functions to sort the array:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static int FindSecondSmallest(int[] arr, int left, int right)
    {
        if (left == right)
            return int.MaxValue;

        if (right - left == 1)
            return Math.Min(arr[left], arr[right]);

        int mid = (left + right) / 2;
        int leftSecondSmallest = FindSecondSmallest(arr, left, mid);
        int rightSecondSmallest = FindSecondSmallest(arr, mid + 1, right);

        return Math.Min(leftSecondSmallest, rightSecondSmallest);
    }

    static int FindSecondSmallest(int[] arr)
    {
        int n = arr.Length;
        int smallest = int.MaxValue;
        int secondSmallest = int.MaxValue;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        {
            if (arr[i] < smallest)
            {
                secondSmallest = smallest;
                smallest = arr[i];
            }
            else if (arr[i] < secondSmallest && arr[i] != smallest)
            {
                secondSmallest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        return secondSmallest;
    }

    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        int[] arr = { 5, 8, 1, 3, 9, 4, 2, 7, 6 };

        int secondSmallest = FindSecondSmallest(arr);
        Console.WriteLine("Second Smallest Element: " + secondSmallest);

        int secondSmallestUsingDC = FindSecondSmallest(arr, 0, arr.Length - 1);
        Console.WriteLine("Second Smallest Element (using divide and conquer): " + secondSmallestUsingDC);
    }
}
```

In this program, we have defined two methods - `FindSecondSmallest` and `Main`. 

The `FindSecondSmallest` method without parameters uses a simple iterative approach to find the second smallest element in the array. It initializes `smallest` and `secondSmallest` variables to `int.MaxValue` and iterates over the array, updating the values of `smallest` and `secondSmallest` as necessary. Finally, it returns the value of `secondSmallest`.

The `FindSecondSmallest` method with parameters implements a divide and conquer algorithm to find the second smallest element in the array. It takes in the array `arr`, and the left and right indices indicating the portion of the array to consider. 

In the divide and conquer approach, we first check the base cases where there are only two or one elements in the considered portion of the array. If there is only one element, we return `int.MaxValue` as there is no second smallest element. If there are two elements, we return the minimum of the two elements.

If neither of the base cases apply, we find the mid point of the portion of the array, and recursively call `FindSecondSmallest` on the left and right halves of the array. The `leftSecondSmallest` and `rightSecondSmallest` variables store the second smallest elements in their respective halves. Finally, we return the minimum of these two values.

In the `Main` method, we create an array `arr` with some sample values. We then call both versions of the `FindSecondSmallest` method and display the results.

