- We iterate through each character in the input string. For each character, we get its ASCII value and check if `charSet[val]` is already `true`. If it is, that means the character has already occurred before, so we return false.
- If the character hasn't occurred before, we set `charSet[val]` to `true`.
- After iterating through all the characters, if we haven't returned false, that means all the characters in the string are unique, so we return true.

The time complexity of this function is O(n) because we iterate through each character in the input string once. The space complexity is O(1) because we use a fixed-size array of size 128 (assuming ASCII character set), which is independent of the input size.

