```csharp
using System;

public class Program
{
    public static void Main()
    {
        // Get current timestamp in ticks
        long ticks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

        // Convert ticks to hexadecimal
        string hex = ConvertToHex(ticks);

        Console.WriteLine("Random Hexadecimal Value: " + hex);
    }

    public static string ConvertToHex(long value)
    {
        // Define hexadecimal characters
        char[] hexChars = "0123456789ABCDEF".ToCharArray();

        // Initialize a string builder
        char[] hex = new char[16];

        // Convert the value to hexadecimal
        for (int i = 0; i < hex.Length; i++)
        {
            hex[hex.Length - 1 - i] = hexChars[value & 0xF];
            value >>= 4;
        }

        // Return the hexadecimal string
        return new string(hex);
    }
}
```

In this code, we first get the current timestamp in ticks using `DateTime.Now.Ticks`. Then, we define an array of hexadecimal characters. We iterate over the ticks value and extract each nibble (4 bits) using bitwise AND operator `&` with `0xF` (which is equivalent to decimal 15). We then shift the value right by 4 bits to get the next nibble. This process continues until we have converted all the nibbles to hexadecimal characters. Finally, we return the hexadecimal string.

Note: This code generates a random hexadecimal value based on the current timestamp in ticks, but it may not be cryptographically secure for generating random numbers.

