Here's the modified PascalABC.NET program to count all the vowels in a given string, ignoring vowels followed by a consonant and vowels enclosed within parentheses:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        string str = "This is a (sample) string.";
        int vowelCount = CountVowels(str);
        Console.WriteLine("Total Vowels: " + vowelCount);
    }

    static int CountVowels(string str)
    {
        string vowels = "aeiou";
        int count = 0;
        bool ignoreNextConsonant = false;
        bool ignoreVowelsInParentheses = false;

        for (int i = 0; i < str.Length; i++)
        {
            char c = char.ToLower(str[i]);

            if (c == '(')
            {
                ignoreVowelsInParentheses = true;
            }
            else if (c == ')')
            {
                ignoreVowelsInParentheses = false;
            }
            else if (ignoreVowelsInParentheses && vowels.Contains(c.ToString()))
            {
                // Ignore vowels within parentheses
                continue;
            }
            else if (vowels.Contains(c.ToString()))
            {
                if (ignoreNextConsonant)
                {
                    ignoreNextConsonant = false;
                    continue;
                }

                count++;

                // Check if the next character is a consonant
                if (i < str.Length - 1 && !vowels.Contains(char.ToLower(str[i + 1]).ToString()))
                {
                    ignoreNextConsonant = true;
                }
            }
        }

        return count;
    }
}
```

The program keeps track of whether the next consonant should be ignored using the `ignoreNextConsonant` boolean flag. It also keeps track of whether vowels should be ignored within parentheses using the `ignoreVowelsInParentheses` boolean flag.

In the `CountVowels` method, the program iterates through each character of the string and checks if it is a vowel. If it is a vowel, it increments the count and checks if the next character is a consonant. If the next character is a consonant, the program sets the `ignoreNextConsonant` flag to true, which will skip the next consonant. The program also checks if the character is within parentheses and whether vowels should be ignored within parentheses. If the character is within parentheses and vowels should be ignored, it continues to the next character without incrementing the count.

Finally, the program returns the count of vowels found in the string.

